# Actor Pipeline Rule

For non-trivial multi-file or mass-failure work, follow the project actor pipeline instead of a single monolithic agent session.

## Load these skills

- `.cursor/skills/actor-pipeline/SKILL.md`
- `.cursor/skills/blind-peer-review/SKILL.md`

## Agent prompts

- `docs/agents/producer-worker-agent.md`
- `docs/agents/blind-reviewer-agent.md`
- `docs/agents/fixer-agent.md`
- `docs/agents/error-shard-agent.md`
- `docs/agents/test-shard-agent.md`

## Scripts

- `python scripts/agent_pipeline/parse_failures.py`
- `python scripts/agent_pipeline/worktree_pool.py`
- `python scripts/agent_pipeline/shard_tests.py`
- `python scripts/agent_pipeline/merge_worktree.py`

## Gates

- `ruff check` on touched paths
- `python scripts/run_tests.py` for assigned tests/shards

## Hard constraints

- Reviewers are fresh Task subagents with no parent history (spec + diff only).
- Parallel fix agents each get their own git worktree under `.worktrees/`.
- Do not merge dirty or failing worktrees.
